**What changed:** The signals-forms `[field]` binding instructions (`ɵɵcontrolCreate`, `ɵɵcontrol` in `packages/core/src/render3/instructions/control.ts`) now classify the control host once during the first create pass and cache the result in new `TNodeFlags` bits — `isFormControl = 0x400`, `isFormValueControl = 0x800`, `isFormCheckboxControl = 0x1000`, `isNativeNumericControl = 0x2000`, `isNativeTextControl = 0x4000` — instead of re-deriving it on every create/update pass via `getControlDirective`/`getCustomControlComponent`/`isNativeControl`/`isNumericInput`/`isTextInput` (`isTextInput` was renamed to `isTextControl`) (https://github.com/angular/angular/commit/32f86d35f7cd177b6e4525a7ae97909888d9fee4). The internal runtime error code `RuntimeErrorCode.INVALID_CONTROL_HOST` (numeric code `318`, unchanged) was renamed to `RuntimeErrorCode.INVALID_FIELD_DIRECTIVE_HOST`, and the thrown message changed from `'<div>' is an invalid control host. The host must be a native form control (such as <input>', '<select>', or '<textarea>') or a custom form control component with a 'value' or 'checked' model.` to `'<div>' is an invalid [field] directive host. The host must be a native form control …` (same file, `packages/core/src/errors.ts`, goldens `goldens/public-api/core/errors.api.md`).

